{"object":"Open-circuit voltage, internal resistance and dynamic voltage drops; internal resistance rises significantly at low temperature. This is a generic model rather than a measurement of the worker's phone.","predicate":"depends_on","source_url":"http://localhost:8090/content/wikipedia_en_all_nopic/Equivalent_circuit_model_for_Li-ion_cells","subject":"lithium-ion loaded terminal voltage","text":"A lithium-ion equivalent-circuit model separates open-circuit voltage from loaded terminal voltage, includes resistance and dynamic voltage drops, and says internal resistance rises significantly at low temperature. This makes a cold load-related voltage collapse plausible but does not measure the worker's phone or its exact state of charge.","title":"prop_liion_low_temp_terminal_voltage"}